2-2) set_user_override

The set_user_override function takes a user_id, a feature name, and an enabled boolean value. It should add or update a feature override for that user, following these rules:

The user must already have an assigned plan.
The feature must be defined in at least one subscription plan, though not necessarily the user's own plan.
The enabled value is always a boolean and may explicitly enable or disable the feature.
If the user already has an override for the feature, replace it.
Return true if the override is added or updated. Return false if the user has no assigned plan, or if the feature is not defined in any plan.

